    {
      "id": "290218c1-7eee-5f0d-9a73-70038714912b",
      "name": "Guide: Archive attachments with saved receipts",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        0,
        -170
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Archive attachments with saved receipts\nFor **Folderit Tailor-plan users** with API credentials. Requires an n8n release with Data Table node v1.1; tested runtime: n8n 2.42.5. [Install and connect Folderit](https://www.folderit.com/knowledge-base/connect-folderit-to-n8n/)\n\nRun **folderit-ledger-setup.json** once in the same n8n project. Copy its table ID into Settings. All copies processing the same source/destination must use the SAME table. Choose Folderit credentials in every Folderit node. Never put secrets in Settings.\n\nImport **folderit-failure-alert-email.json**, configure its SMTP connection, save it, then select it in this workflow's **⋯ → Settings → Error workflow**. Error workflows must be tested using an activated workflow; manual runs do not trigger them.\n\nConnect your IMAP credential in the trigger. Use a dedicated intake mailbox with TLS; existing unseen messages can be fetched on the first run. Read/unread status is unchanged. Messages without a stable Message-ID are held for inspection.\n\nSet all Settings placeholders, then select the same Folderit credential in Upload attachment, Read uploaded document and Download stored attachment. mailboxScope must remain a stable label for this mailbox. Configure allowedExtensions. Multiple permitted attachments are processed one at a time. Test a replay and confirm no second file appears.",
        "width": 1100,
        "height": 650
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "1b6b3a5e-32fe-59a3-a904-2e1ed90afa14",
      "name": "Guide: Recovery and limits",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "typeVersion": 1,
      "position": [
        1180,
        -170
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "content": "# Recovery and limits\nThe table contains a single processing lock plus durable receipts. Only a run owning the lock may perform an upload or send a message. A completed receipt suppresses repeats for its key. The lock has NO automatic expiry: a crash, failed readback or uncertain API response keeps work blocked for inspection.\n\nCompeting runs wait and retry lock acquisition for about one minute; uploads/messages are never automatically retried. If a run still reports a busy lock, retry that FAILED execution after the owner finishes. Do not discard its input. On other failures, inspect saved executions, receipt state and the actual destination. Never clear the lock while its owner may still be running. Reconcile pending rows before clearing it. See CUSTOMER-WORKFLOWS.md for recovery steps.\n\nThis is duplicate protection with explicit recovery, not an exactly-once guarantee across n8n and an external service. Keep failed execution/binary data long enough for recovery and monitor the failure-alert workflow itself. Production provider delivery and fresh Cloud behavior require validation in your environment.\n\nOne receipt key includes account, destination, mailbox, message ID, attachment field, filename and SHA-256. A new email can intentionally archive identical content. Every new upload is downloaded again and its bytes hashed before completion is recorded; this adds download traffic and avoids depending on asynchronously populated server hash metadata. Empty files and files over 100 MiB fail. Extension checks do not replace malware scanning. No automatic upload retries.",
        "width": 1050,
        "height": 650
      }
    }
  ],
